WEBVTT

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.930
Oh, good morning!

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.740
Good morning!

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.610
Off to work?

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.480
It must be hard, having to get up 
this early on your day off.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.450
Same for you!

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.450
How's Kotori-chan doing?

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.040
Think she'll be okay on her own?

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.260
I think I'm putting her through a lot.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.600
But you know, lately a teacher from her 
school's been coming to check on her.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.340
It's a huge help!

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.300
That's what she said.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.280
I didn't know there were any 
good teachers like that anymore.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.310
She hasn't told me about it!

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.460
She hasn't told her! She hasn't told her!

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.940
If you're done with your cups,
bring them over here.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.330
I'll wash them!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.520
Later!

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:53.610
Anyone who doesn't help 
clean up gets no snacks!

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.860
Five seconds!

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.630
Four! Three! Two! One!

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.400
Whoa!

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.080
Good.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.460
A teacher, huh?

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.800
I'll finish this.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.200
Here.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.480
Take these to Kotori-chan 
and see how she's doing.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.600
Is she in the restaurant?

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.650
Hey, I'm coming i—

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:37.910
Hello.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.820
Uh...

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.740
Oh, no, I just, um... I mean...

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.440
Welcome!

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.920
I'm Inuzuka Tsumugi!

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.460
Hello.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.840
I'm Kojika Shinobu.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.500
A customer!

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.200
Daddy! It's a customer!

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.160
What's going on?

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.500
I-I'll explain...

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.480
<b>A Gyoza Party with Friends</b>

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.570
So that's it?

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.160
Yes.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.200
You should've told me!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:41.740
Yes!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.180
Why?!

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.960
Why didn't you tell me?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.620
Treat me like a friend!

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.620
Treat?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.800
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.120
I thought you'd be busy 
helping out around the house!

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.340
Also, I don't know who this teacher is.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.540
I've never seen him.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.480
That's probably because you're in Class D,

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.970
and your math teacher is Kumagaya-sensei.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.330
No, it's more like you're just so plain, 
you're hard to remember.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.380
Shinobu...

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:07.350
Anyway,

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.360
if you want to learn more about cooking,

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.770
I'll help you!

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.620
Leave it to me!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.250
But aren't you too busy?

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:16.940
Not really!

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.620
It's only a few times a month, right?

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.140
Are you okay with this, Sensei?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.420
If both your parents are okay with it,

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.310
I'm in no position to complain.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.520
I see.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.660
What?

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:34.250
I'm going to help make food, too!

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.650
You'll have more members!

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.960
Like a party!

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.550
A p-party?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.480
A party!

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.680
Okay, let's decide on a date for now.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.220
It'll make it easier to tell our parents.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.010
Does our next day off sound good?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.650
Goodnight!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.060
Goodnight, Tsumugi.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.160
A party...

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.110
Hello!

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.830
I'm Tanabe, the sitter!

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.680
Thank you for coming!

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.880
Tsumugi-chan, the sitter's here.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.760
Hop, hop, hop!

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.280
You're in a good mood today, 
huh, Tsumugi-chan?

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.770
Hey, can we stop by Yagi-chan's place?

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.470
Sure, but why?

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.980
Oh, you know...

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.270
I'm back.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.860
Tsumugi?

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.740
What's this?

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:47.490
Did you make it at school?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.950
<b>Invitation
June 18th
Party!</b>

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.150
It was still a secret.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.450
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.510
Tsumugi-san, what might this be?

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.420
Well, it's an invitation!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.090
Invitation?

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:03.070
Kotori-chan, and Shinobu-chan,

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:07.510
and Daddy, and my friends 
from school, and Yagi-cha—

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.760
Tsumugi, you can't invite 
your friends from school.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.580
But they said it was a party.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.200
Don't you bring your friends to parties?

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:19.900
Yes.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:24.230
But you know, Tsumugi, we'll be 
eating at Iida-san's place, right?

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.240
Iida?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.510
K-Kotori-san's house.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:29.490
Oh.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.860
And she doesn't know your friends, right?

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.200
Probably not...

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.650
If a bunch of strange kids she didn't invite

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.970
showed up at her house 
all of a sudden for a party,

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:43.450
what would she and her parents think?

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:46.090
Th-That it would be fun?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.370
Um...

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:53.640
It's not good to send out invitiations 
without talking to Kotori-chan's family.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.490
Are you mad, Daddy?

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:58.780
I'm... not mad.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:06:59.600
It's just...

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.350
<b>Invitation
June 18th
Party!</b>

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.350
Daddy doesn't want to cause trouble

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.540
for another family.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:09.110
I can't invite my friends?

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.710
Everyone, snacktime!

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.880
These look good!

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.080
They are good!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.500
Mommy's snacks are always good!

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.210
Yeah!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.750
You try some too, Kouhei-san.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.390
Yum!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:37.390
Then... What'll we do?

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:46.170
Well, how about we put a sticker 
on top of this date with a new date,

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.820
<b>Invitation
June 18th
Party!</b>

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:52.250
and invite your friends from 
school to our house instead?

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.130
They can come here?

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:58.440
Of course.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.580
We'll have to ask their parents first,

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.410
but it's been a while, so let's invite them over.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.470
Yay!

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.080
Then what about this one?

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:12.190
The one with Kotori-chan and Shinobu-chan!

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.130
Of course, we'll do that one 
just like we planned.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.640
Which means...

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:24.440
<b>First Time</b>

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.150
<b>Second Time</b>

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.650
Two... parties?

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.110
My head went "boom"!

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.370
A tomato and a gyoza?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.080
No!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.860
It's a heart and a moon!

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.520
If it were a gyoza, I'd eat it!

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.000
Okay, okay.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:47.540
Gyoza...

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.040
Gyoza, huh?

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.050
Uh-oh...

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:54.430
My mouth's all filled with drool.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:58.060
<b>Party</b>

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.270
You've turned into quite the 
big eater, huh, Tsumugi?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.020
Gyoza?!

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.300
Y-Yes...

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:05.890
Is that okay?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.470
Of course it is!

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:09.400
Gyoza gets me excited!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:12.690
Just thinking about it 
fills my mouth with drool.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.050
Okay, let's do it, then.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.700
Sure. I'll ask my mom for the recipe.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.160
Please tell Kojika-san, too.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.640
Oh, okay.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.210
<b>Kojika Greengrocers</b>

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.210
Gyoza, huh? Sounds great!

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.030
Yeah.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.120
Gyoza is so exciting, right?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.100
Yup!

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.500
What's exciting?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.040
Nothing.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.370
What do you want for snacks?

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.360
Pancakes!

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.420
Big ones!

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.080
Okay, I'll go make you some. 
Wash your hands and wait.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:40.970
Yeah!

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.080
You want some too, Kotori?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.380
No, that's okay...

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:45.870
Don't be shy!

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.100
One more person doesn't change anything!

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:50.410
Yeah, thanks.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.720
But I'm okay.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.780
I need to bring in the laundry before it rains.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:55.570
Bye!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.370
Let me handle the veggies!

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.960
I'll bring you the best we've got!

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:00.710
Okay!

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.850
I'm here!

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.920
Oh, already? You're early.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.080
Hello!

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.600
Glad to have your help.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.940
Here are the veggies!

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.010
I brought us good stuff!

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.220
I'll wash them all.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.320
Right, right.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.780
Huh? Where's Kotori?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.820
Oh, she's in the bathroom right now.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.320
Maybe I'm a bad person.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.550
Kotori-chan!

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:58.090
Tsumugi, wait!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.120
Oh, it's all right.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:00.920
What is it?

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.510
Here! It's your invitation!

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.370
For today!

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.890
It says I want you to come!

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.230
I made it!

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.230
Look, look, Kotori!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.900
I got one, too!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.400
That's a heart. Not a peach.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.900
The girls get hearts!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.910
Yeah, yeah! It's a great heart!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.280
That makes me so happy.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.590
Thank you, Tsumugi-chan.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:29.640
Thank you!

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.420
It was nothing!

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.120
Who's that?

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:44.260
Hello.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.270
Tsumugi, you didn't...

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.910
I forgot I invited Yagi-chan, too!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.270
Will that cause trouble?

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.120
Huh?

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.900
Oh, it's okay! No problem at all!

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:55.940
The owner isn't in?

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.350
My mom's out at work.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.900
Well, if I'm not supposed to be here...

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.400
Oh, come on, it's fine!

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.370
You've got an invitation, right? 
And we've got the ingredients.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.640
I'm sorry. Is this okay?

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.830
Yes, it's really fine!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.040
Let's have a gyoza party today!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.710
We'll start with the shells!

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.040
Okay!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:15.950
Are we cool?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.420
I guess. Thanks.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.580
It's nothing.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.570
It looks like this won't go to waste.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:26.090
<b>Strong Flour</b>

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:26.090
First, pass the flour through a sieve,

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.260
dissolve the salt in water,

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.680
and add it gradually to the sieved flour

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.210
as you mix thoroughly.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:33.880
Okay!

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.520
It's getting sticky.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:42.880
Now you mix the dough with your hands,

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.680
and form it into a clump.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:50.840
Then dust your working surface 
with flour and knead thoroughly.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.420
Keep folding it on top of itself.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.700
How much?

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:58.890
A hundred times or so.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:04.650
Now, let it sit for 30 minutes.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.520
Okay. What's next?

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.080
We make the an.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.250
The an?

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:11.230
It's what we call the gyoza's filling.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:11.820
Filling?

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:13.230
What goes inside.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.190
Let's see...

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.990
Mince the napa cabbage...

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:21.310
Oh, there's regular cabbage, 
but it's not in the recipe.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:22.800
Oh, the cabbage.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.950
I had a good head of it, so I figured 
we could split it 50/50 with the napa.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:26.940
Let me see that.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.280
Shinobu, it's not in the recipe. Is that okay?

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.710
It's fine!

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.830
I-Is it?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.830
Let's split up the work.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.380
Cut the napa into slightly bigger pieces...

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.380
I'm cutting the cabbage.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.160
Mix with the salt and let it sit.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:45.850
S-Salt?

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:48.170
It draws out the moisture.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.180
You do the cabbage.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.720
On it. Did you cut the chives, 
green onions, and ginger?

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.220
Hey!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:57.270
That's right! They can't cook!

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:59.230
Wow!

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:01.790
It's like a cooking show!

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.220
You can do it too, Daddy!

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:05.110
Leave it to me!

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:08.140
If I just stay calm...

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:12.330
For the green onion, make several cuts 
along the stem with the knife,

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.800
so it looks like a broom...

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.620
You can do it! You can do it! Daddy!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.530
You can do it! You can do it! Daddy!

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.090
Then turn it to the side...

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:22.510
You can do it!

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.780
You do this, Kotori.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.820
Mix up the ground pork.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.600
Knead it, knead it!

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.510
Then, once it gets sticky,

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.350
add the seasonings...

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:39.350
and all the dried vegetables from before.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:42.770
Then add the sesame oil, 
and when it looks good,

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.210
put it in the fridge for a while.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:45.960
Okay!

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.240
Now it's finally time for the shells!

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.740
I laid a tarp over the tatami mats,

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.250
so we can do it here.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.490
Good thinking!

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:57.120
So big!

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:00.730
Tsumugi, this isn't our house.
Don't play around.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.130
Okay!

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.120
Were you just doing something?

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.470
Yeah, I tore off a chunk of dough 
in an easy-to-handle size,

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.600
then rolled it into a cylinder to 
chop it up into small pieces.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.750
I'll dust the ends.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.320
So, um, you do what with the dough?

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.230
Sorry, can you tell us again?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.320
Tear off an easy-to-handle chunk of dough,

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:25.340
about like this.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:27.980
Roll it into a cylinder,

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:31.660
then chop it into little pieces.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.830
Powder the cut bits with flour and they 
won't stick when you stretch them out.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:40.300
Um, can you do that slower?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.540
Sorry.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:45.450
Okay, once you've cut it small, you do this...

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.160
Then this...

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:49.270
Then this.

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:51.670
Simple, right?

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.480
Well, learn by doing.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:55.820
Are we about ready?

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.560
Next, how to fill them.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:02.060
Put the an in the center, 
then wet the edge with water.

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:05.700
Fold the sides together, then add creases...

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.420
And it's done.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.850
Let's split up and have some 
stretch out the shells,

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:13.790
and the others fill them.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:16.400
Okay! I'm gonna fill them!

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:19.630
Okay, I'll keep making the shells, 
so you keep filling them!

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:20.500
Okay!

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.750
So thin!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.670
I like this! It's fun!

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.180
It's so slippery! It feels neat!

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.380
Here, Tsumugi.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.100
Put it in the center...

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:38.350
Here's the water.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:48.600
It's done!

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.400
It's done!

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:50.900
Yeah!

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.650
Great job!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.470
I have to do my best, too!

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:58.640
I wanna be able to tell which ones I made!

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:01.420
Well, then... What should we do?

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:03.660
I know!

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:07.540
Take this, and go like this...

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:09.290
Here!

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.650
A ribbon!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.600
I wanna ribbon!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.050
Want to do it with Daddy?

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:17.840
Yup!

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:18.730
There.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:23.120
Ribbon, Tsumugi's ribbon, bon, bon...

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.230
Bon, bon, bon!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.420
Daddy's is done, too!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.560
Combine!

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:30.520
It's done!

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.350
Look, Kotori-chan!

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.150
It turned out so cute!

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.940
I'm gonna keep making more!

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:42.270
Yagi-chan, keep making the shells!

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.770
We're gonna catch up to you!

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.710
Hey, that's the spirit!

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:48.730
Kotori, come here a sec.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.050
Shinobu?

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:58.420
What's wrong?

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.920
Uh, yeah... Well...

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.220
Do you...

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.640
W-Was I acting weird?

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.500
But, um... Well, it's because...

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.820
Was this important to you?

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.820
Er, I mean... No, it's...

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:13.750
Huh?

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:18.030
Doing things like this slowly and carefully 
with Sensei and his daughter.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.150
I'm always in a hurry,

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.540
and I always want to interfere...

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.900
So I thought maybe I did something wrong.

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:27.290
Of course not...

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:31.040
I mean, you were smiling so much.

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:39.420
Yeah... It's important to me.

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:41.760
It's something I want to treasure.

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:44.140
I see.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:48.810
But it was a lot of fun having you here today!

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.470
It's true!

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:53.310
You're so silly.

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:55.820
You guys are late.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:57.550
They're cooking already.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.860
Sorry we didn't wait for you.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.270
What?!

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:05.160
This guy's terrible! He doesn't get it!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.840
I don't get what?

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:07.790
Huh?!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.210
You cook them, Sensei!

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.250
Hey, what are you... Wait... Wait a...

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.320
Okay!

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.500
You can do it, Daddy!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.580
Go, go, Daddy!

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.580
Hey, I'm your elder, you know.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:18.940
That's not what this is for!

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:21.480
Don't you think natural monuments 
should be preserved?

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.080
Huh?

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:22.720
Look!

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.770
You can do it! You can do it!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.030
You think that's long enough?

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:29.580
I think it is.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:30.410
Okay...

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.770
Done!

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.980
Wow!

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:46.600
I'm stuck in this role again?

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:50.870
Oh, yeah! We've got these, too!

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:52.600
Gyoza?

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:54.330
They look different!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.810
Since we made them from scratch,

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:59.260
I thought we could make boiled gyoza, too.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.040
The shells get all chewy. They're so good!

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.640
We still have some an left.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:07.080
I brought chicken wings, too.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.870
We'll make chicken wing gyoza.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.120
What's that? What's that?

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:15.530
The gyoza shells are meat, too!

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.270
Wow! Wow!

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.080
Yagi-chan's like a restaurant guy!

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.080
I do work at a restaurant.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.490
This is on our menu.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.620
It's a gyoza party!

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.380
Let's eat!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.850
No spicy sauce for Tsumugi-chan, right?

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.520
Yummy!

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.960
This is so good!

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.220
What are these again?

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.410
Boiled gyoza.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.250
The shells are all shiny!

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:12.250
Right? Crazy, huh?

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.450
Man, I'd love a beer.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.330
I'm glad they came out so well.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.920
Thanks, Shinobu.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.130
Let's do it again, okay?

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:27.820
Ahh!

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:28.680
Nah.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.680
I'm busy, you know.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.340
I'll do it once you guys get a little better.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:35.870
Shino—

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.650
Hey! Is my gyoza good?

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:44.990
It's great!

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:49.240
Daddy and Kotori-chan, 
you eat my gyoza, too!

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.180
Okay!

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:52.490
Let's eat!

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:56.000
It's so good!

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.580
Right?
